on that biden  supporters are way likely  way more likely to vote by mail is they  are taking the risk  of catching coronavirus more seriously  than republicans  now you could come in and say well if  there's more vote by mail open more  trump supporters will vote by mail  if there's less vote by mail open biden  supporters  will just go and vote in person it's all  going to shake out evenly  that's exactly the wrong approach  that is exactly the mistake that's being  made in analyzing this  biden voters are more likely not to vote  at all if they can't do it safely  while trump voters are more likely to  vote in person  if that's available if that's all that's  available so  sure most biden voters planning to vote  by mail  if they are told you can't vote by mail  they'll put a mask on  they understand the importance they'll  go and  take the risk because they understand  the importance of the election  but if you believe as is probably the  case that there are  some biden supporters who might not vote  at all if they can't vote absentee  you then try to stop vote by mail  altogether which is exactly what donald  trump is doing  imagine that if you take some state that  could be close  and you restrict cancel or stop vote by  mail  and it dissuades just three percent of  the total electorate from voting  and imagine that in that three percent  who will say  if i can't vote by mail i'm not voting  at all imagine that  80 of that slice would have voted for  biden  and 20 of that slice would have voted  for donald trump  that can flip a state that it literally  is enough to flip a state let's look at  wisconsin in 2016. now  trump won wisconsin in 2016 very  narrowly trump won by about 22 000 votes  in 2016 in wisconsin if you dissuade  three percent  from voting that's about 83 000 people  that you would dissuade from voting  maybe if you say you have to come in in  person  if 80 of those dissuaded or biden  supporters  and 20 of those dissuaded are trump  supporters